<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19708" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glūtĭno</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		gluten, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to glue</i>, <i>glue together.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">chartas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 25, 60, § 127</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fragmenta vitri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					29, 3, 11, § 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in medic., <i>to close
				up</i>, <i>join</i> an opening, esp. a wound: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glutinantia medicamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 7,
					4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cicatricibus glutinandis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					33, 6, 35, § 105</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecisos nervos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					25, 5, 19, § 43</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cels. 7, 28</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si orae vulneris se glutinarunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					27 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
